  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn [merge existing and new import maps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#merge-existing-and-new-import-maps), it specifies **deep copy** of the newImportMap's **scopes** map and **imports** map.\n\n> 1. Let newImportMapScopes be a deep copy of newImportMap's [scopes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-import-map-scopes).\n\n...\n\n> 3. Let newImportMapImports be a deep copy of newImportMap's [imports](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-import-map-imports).\n\nWith the **_Note_** saying\n\n> We're mutating these copies and removing items from them when they are used to ignore scope-specific rules. This is true for newImportMapScopes, as well as to newImportMapImports below.\n\nBut the newImportMap comes from the [create an import map parsed result](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#create-an-import-map-parse-result)\nand I think from the current spec, you can't reuse the same import map parsed result in another global, so it looks like the 'deep copy' is redudant.\n",
